[[File:Sant_Cristofor_skyline.png|300px|left|Sant Cristòfor]]

'''[[Sant Cristòfor]]''' is the capital and largest city of [[Balboa]], and the principal city of the Sant Cristòfor comarca. With a population of approximately 5.16 million, it is the largest city in Balboa and one of the major economic and financial centres of [[Abyala]]. Situated on the Badia de Sant Cristòfor — a U-shaped bay on the Shendan Ocean coast of the [[Isthmus of Balboa]] — the city is composed of a peninsula and the mainland area that wraps around the bay, and is divided into 11 ciutats, each with its own local council.

Inhabited for millennia by the Birú at the western terminus of the principal trans-isthmian portage route, Sant Cristòfor became a cosmopolitan entrepôt under Volisanian colonial rule and later the [[Zong Balboa|Zong administration's]] "Shining Star" era — a period of rapid growth, cultural flourishing, and relative egalitarianism. The city's distinctive urban culture — the syncretic ''[[istmo son]]'' musical tradition, the emergence of [[Balboan Creole]], and the mixing of Illypnian, Fosian, Kaftian, and indigenous influences — developed across this cosmopolitan colonial period. Today, Sant Cristòfor is the principal financial hub of Balboa, accounting for roughly 63% of national GDP, and remains one of the most ethnically diverse cities in Abyala.

